{"descriptionModels":[{"description":"You master the shortsword, longsword, scimitar, rapier, and greatsword as well as their variations (katana, zweihander, etc). You gain the following benefits:\n\n- Increase your Dexterity or Strength score by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n\n- You gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls you make with a weapon mastered by this feat.\n\n- When you end your turn, you can assume a parrying stance, provided you have a weapon mastered by this feat in hand. Until the start of your next turn, you can use your reaction to make one melee attack with that weapon against a creature that attacks you with a melee attack. If your attack roll is higher than that of your opponent, the creature misses it\u0027s attack. You resolve the roll after the creature\u0027s attack but before any result is decided.\n\n- When you make an attack with a weapon mastered by this feat as a reaction, you have advantage on the attack roll.","level":1}],"id":"Custom3966ec56-5650-45ae-a60e-aed58c1edfc9","isFeature":false,"jsonType":"feat","level":1,"name":"Blade Mastery [NPHB] [SM]","notes":"","type":"Feat"}